.TH KENTSCRIPT-FFI 3 "KentScript Manual"
.SH NAME
kentscript-ffi \- KentScript Foreign Function Interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B let lib = ffi_load("libc.so.6");
.br
let printf = ffi_call(lib, "printf", "Hello %s\\n", "World");
.SH DESCRIPTION
The FFI (Foreign Function Interface) allows KentScript to call functions in C libraries directly.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
\fBffi_load(path: str) -> lib\fR
Load a C shared library by path. Returns a library handle.
.br
\fBExample:\fR let libc = ffi_load("/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6");
.TP
\fBffi_call(lib, func: str, *args) -> any\fR
Call a function from a loaded library. Arguments are automatically converted to C types.
.br
\fBExample:\fR ffi_call(libc, "printf", "Value: %d\\n", 42);
.TP
\fBffi_c_int(val) -> c_int\fR
Create C integer.
.TP
\fBffi_c_long(val) -> c_long\fR
Create C long.
.TP
\fBffi_c_float(val) -> c_float\fR
Create C float.
.TP
\fBffi_c_double(val) -> c_double\fR
Create C double.
.TP
\fBffi_c_char_p(val: str) -> c_char_p\fR
Create C string (char*).
.TP
\fBffi_c_void_p(val: int) -> c_void_p\fR
Create C void pointer.
.TP
\fBffi_c_bool(val: bool) -> c_bool\fR
Create C boolean.
.TP
\fBffi_sizeof(ctype: str) -> int\fR
Get size of C type.
.TP
\fBffi_addressof(obj) -> int\fR
Get address of C object.
.TP
\fBffi_cast(obj, ctype: str)\fR
Cast pointer to different type.
.TP
\fBffi_string(ptr, size=null) -> str\fR
Convert C string to KentScript string.
.TP
\fBffi_array(ctype: str, size: int)\fR
Create C array.
.TP
\fBffi_struct(fields: dict) -> struct\fR
Create C struct.
.TP
\fBffi_struct_c(fields: dict, pack=null) -> struct\fR
Create C struct with \fBrepr(C)\fR layout.
.TP
\fBffi_pointer(obj) -> pointer\fR
Create C pointer.
.TP
\fBffi_byref(obj) -> byref\fR
Create reference for passing to functions.
.TP
\fBffi_callback(restype, argtypes, func) -> callback\fR
Create C callback from KentScript function.
.TP
\fBffi_call_safe(lib, func: str, argtypes: list, restype: str, *args) -> result\fR
Call function with type checking and error handling.
.TP
\fBffi_parse_header(header_path: str) -> dict\fR
Parse C header file and return type/function definitions.
.TP
\fBffi_generate_bindings(header_path: str, lib_path: str) -> dict\fR
Generate FFI bindings from C header.
.SH CALLBACKS
FFI callbacks allow passing KentScript functions to C code:
.TP
Example: Create callback for qsort comparison
.br
func compare_int(a: *void, b: *void) -> int {
.br
    let av = ptr_read(a, 4);
.br
    let bv = ptr_read(b, 4);
.br
    return av - bv;
.br
}
.br
let cmp = ffi_callback(ffi_c_int(0), [ffi_c_void_p, ffi_c_void_p], compare_int);
.SH STRUCTS
.TP
Creating C structs:
.br
let point = ffi_struct({"x": "c_int", "y": "c_int"});
.br
point.x = 10;
.br
point.y = 20;
.SH ERROR HANDLING
Use \fBffi_call_safe\fR for error handling:
.TP
let result = ffi_call_safe(libc, "printf", ["c_char_p"], "c_int", "Test %d\\n", 42);
.br
if result.error {
.br
    println("Error: " + result.error);
.br
} else {
.br
    println("Result: " + str(result.result));
.br
}
.SH NOTES
- FFI requires unsafe block for pointer operations
- Always check return values for errors
- Remember to free resources when done
.SH EXAMPLE
:: Load C library
.br
let libc = ffi_load("/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6");
.br

:: Call printf
.br
unsafe {
.br
    ffi_call(libc, "printf", "Hello from C!\n");
.br
}
.br

:: Call with return value
.br
let result = ffi_call(libc, "atoi", "12345");
.br
println("Parsed: " + str(result));  :: 12345
